%%label II. Andante
%%note A flat major. A song for the violins, repeated by clarinet and flute; a middle section in F minor that grows loud and falls back; the song again, lightly ornamented, with the flute above the violins.
X:1
T:Mozart’s Missing Symphony
T:II. Andante
C:Lor, in the manner of Mozart
M:3/4
L:1/8
Q:"Andante" 1/4=72
%%score [fl ob cl bn] hn [v1 v2 va vc cb]
% The score is written at sounding pitch. Dynamics in the wind, horn and double-bass parts are set two or three levels below the strings to balance the playback samples of this site; they are a playback compromise, not dynamics for live players.
V:fl clef=treble name="Fl."
V:ob clef=treble name="Ob."
V:cl clef=treble name="Cl."
V:bn clef=bass name="Bn."
V:hn clef=treble name="Hn."
V:v1 clef=treble name="Vl. I"
V:v2 clef=treble name="Vl. II"
V:va clef=alto name="Vla."
V:vc clef=bass name="Vc."
V:cb clef=bass name="Cb."
K:Ab
V:fl
